<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SUDAN'S BASHIR LEAVES S.AFRICA FOR MOZAMBIQUE.</title>
<headline>SUDAN'S BASHIR LEAVES S.AFRICA FOR MOZAMBIQUE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sudanese President Omar Hassan al-Bashir left South Africa on Wednesday morning after he met President Nelson Mandela on the future of his country.</p>
<p>Bashir on Tuesday called for a ceasefire in the gruelling 14-year civil war with the Sudan People's Liberation Army (SPLA) rebels in the south of the country.</p>
<p>&quot;They left this morning for Mozambique,&quot; said Sudanese Embassy official Hassan Yousif.</p>
</text>
